name unicode-properties-not-in-xml
# The properties that the property files give and the XML does not: Hyphen (PropList.txt), Grapheme_Link
# (DerivedCoreProperties.txt), and Expands_On_NFC, Expands_On_NFD, Expands_On_NFKC, Expands_On_NFKD and FC_NFKC
# (DerivedNormalizationProps.txt). Every other row of these files says what the XML says. A row of a binary
# property writes the code point and the property: that pair is attested. A row of FC_NFKC writes the code point,
# the property and the mapping, which is recorded as the text it is. The files do not name their fields; the
# columns are numbered here only to say where a part is. A row whose code point is a range speaks of the range,
# recorded as the range it is: the path of its first and its last.
match PropList.txt DerivedCoreProperties.txt DerivedNormalizationProps.txt

tier row by \n
comment hash
remark hash
padded
names 0 1 2
tier field by ;

thing row 0
range 0
content 1
codepoints 2
when 1 matches ^(Hyphen|Grapheme_Link|Expands_On_NFC|Expands_On_NFD|Expands_On_NFKC|Expands_On_NFKD)$
pair row 1
always
when 1 is FC_NFKC
relate row 1 to 2
